<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41715" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπι-ψαύω</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ψαυσῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Archim.
					<u>Con.Sph.</u>
					30
				</span></i>
			:—<i>touch on the surface, touch lightly,</i> c.
			gen., <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				217
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.87
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>attain,</i> abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ πᾶν τέλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>I.</u>
					4(3).11
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. φιλοτάτων</span>
			<i>to aspire to</i> loves, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.92
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τινὸς οὐδὲ κατὰ μικρόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phan.Hist.
					19
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆς ἐ.,</span> of shipwrecked
			persons, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				636.2
			</span></i> : generally, <i>handle,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κώπης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1255
				</span></i>
			 ; <i>meddle with,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάφου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					1394
				</span></i>
			 : metaph., also, <i>touch lightly upon,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.65
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> Geom.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -ψαύουσα</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γραμμή</span>) <i>tangent,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Archim.
				<u>Sph.Cyl.</u>
				1.12
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c.dat.,
				<i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				2.456
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> c. acc.,
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				12.551
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> once in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, intr. and metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅς τ᾽ ὀλίγον
				περ ἐπιψαύῃ πραπίδεσσιν</span> who <i>can reach</i>
			ever so little way by his wits, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.547
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
